//     deepLore: `Life in their new forest home presented heavy emotional burdens. Draupadi and Bhima were particularly vocal in expressing their anger at Yudhisthira's unwavering adherence to Kshatriya law and his destructive gambling habits. They held him accountable for their current predicament, and during one heated moment, Bhima even called for fire to burn Yudhisthira's hands in frustration. Arjuna, despite his heartbreak, maintained a sense of acceptance toward their fate, suspecting that Duryodhana's scheme was to utilize the 13 years to amass a formidable army. Nakula and Sahadeva remained steadfastly loyal to their elder brothers, while Yudhisthira was consumed by guilt over their misfortune.\n\nDuring this challenging time, Sage Vyasa came to visit Yudhisthira and offered wise council. He advised Yudhisthira to seek the blessings of Lord Surya, the Sun God, whose radiant energy nourishes all life. The Sun God Surya looked favorably upon the young king and bestowed upon him a remarkable gift: a mystical pot. Surya instructed Yudhisthira to give the pot to Draupadi, explaining its extraordinary properties: any meal prepared in this pot will be inexhaustible throughout the day until Draupadi eats from it, after which the pot will remain empty until the next day, when its magical essence renews with the touch of the sun's rays. Grateful for this divine gift, Yudhisthira returned to his family with the means to feed not only themselves, but also many citizens who had sought refuge with the Pandavas.`,
