//     deepLore: `Sage Vyasa informed Yudhisthira of the Kauravas' preparations to amass a formidable army. Understanding the gravity of the situation, Arjuna was tasked with a vital quest: he would journey to acquire divine weapons from Lord Indra, which would prepare them for the impending battle. Accepting this weighty responsibility, Arjuna bid farewell to his family—sorrow weighing heavily upon him—as he set forth on his journey towards the north and the Himalayas. \n\nArjuna travelled for months, traversing rugged terrains, until he encountered a holy sage engaged in deep meditation. Upon waking, the sage tested Arjuna's resolve, offering him the pleasures of hermitage and heaven, but Arjuna remained steadfast, revealing himself to be an agent of Lord Indra and Lord Shiva. While meditating on Mount Kailash, a wild boar charged at him, and Arjuna released an arrow simultaneously with a mysterious hunter. Claiming the game, a fierce battle of archery erupted between them. Exhausted and realizing his opponent's peerless skill, Arjuna fashioned a clay lingam of Lord Shiva and placed a floral garland upon it. To his astonishment, the garland appeared on the hunter, revealing him to be Lord Shiva. Pleased beyond measure by Arjuna's unmatched valor and devotion, Lord Shiva granted him the catastrophic celestial weapon, the Pashupatastra, warning him never to use it recklessly against lesser foes.`,
