//     deepLore: `In a flash of light, Arjuna was greeted by Lord Indra and the other gods, who blessed him with their divine weapons and invaluable knowledge. A celestial vehicle whisked him away to the realms above, where a grand celebration awaited him with dancers and musicians. Under Indra's guidance, Arjuna learned to wield various weapons and immersed himself in the arts of dance and music taught by Chitrasena the Gandharva. \n\nAmidst these wonders, a radiant apsara named Urvashi grew captivated by Arjuna's handsome and virtuous character. One night, driven by desire, she made her way to his chambers and demanded he satisfy her desires. Taken aback, Arjuna respectfully declined, stating that because she had chosen Puru as a husband and was an ancestor of his lineage, he regarded her with the reverence due to a mother. Urvashi's heartache turned into fury, and trembling with rage, she pronounced a curse upon him: to become impotent and spend his time among females as a dancing eunuch. When Lord Indra learned of this, he comforted Arjuna, assuring him that this curse would serve him well during his final year of exile when he must live incognito.`,
