//     deepLore: `King Dhritarashtra, feeling sorrow for his nephews yet still desiring his son's absolute supremacy, listened as Shakuni manipulated Duryodhana into embarking on a sporting expedition into the forest to camp near the Pandavas and flaunt their opulent wealth. Accompanied by Karna, Shakuni, his wives, and hundreds of guards, Duryodhana set off. While journeying, Duryodhana tried to claim a forest lake for a swimming party, but found it occupied by Chitrasena and his Gandharva forces. \n\nA fierce clash ensued in which Duryodhana's royal guards were soundly defeated and Karna was forced to retreat. Duryodhana and many of his retainers were captured, while his fleeing wives sought refuge in the Pandava camp. Though Bhima scoffed at rescuing their tormentor, Yudhisthira insisted that family ties supersede enmity, and Draupadi urged them to aid their cousin. The Pandavas quickly routed the Gandharvas, and when Arjuna recognized their leader as his former music teacher Chitrasena, Chitrasena released Duryodhana. However, being rescued by the Pandavas only fueled Duryodhana's anger and planted deeper seeds of resentful humiliation.`,
