//     deepLore: `Having completed their 13-year exile—including the crucial final year in disguise at Virata's court without being discovered—the Pandavas officially laid claim to the restoration of Indraprastha. However, Duryodhana, consumed by arrogance and unyielding jealousy, flatly refused to cede even an inch of land without a war. \n\nBoth Duryodhana and Arjuna rushed to Dwaraka to secure Lord Krishna's military backing. Duryodhana arrived first and seated himself at Krishna's head, while Arjuna humbly sat at his feet. When Krishna awoke, he offered them a choice: his invincible Narayani army on one side, or himself on the other—unarmed and committed not to fight. Arjuna unhesitatingly chose Krishna as his guide, leaving Duryodhana overjoyed to claim the massive army. Meanwhile, emissaries and peace talks led by Krishna to Hastinapur ultimately failed against Duryodhana's stubborn defiance.`,
